The statutes of your state include a modern version of the old English statute of frauds, providing as follows:

No contract which . . . by its terms is not to be performed within one year from the date of making thereof . . . shall be enforceable unless the contract or some note or memorandum thereof shall be in writing and signed by the party to be charged.

The statutes of the state of Franklin contain a substantially similar provision.

